# Accounts, cloud save and friends.
#
# This repository already carries a working configuration in .env.production,
# which Vite reads at build time. This file is the template for pointing a
# build at a DIFFERENT Supabase project — copy it to .env.local (ignored by
# git) and fill both values in from Project Settings -> API.
#
# Run supabase/schema.sql in that project's SQL editor first, or the app will
# sign in and then fail to read anything.
#
# Both values are compiled into the bundle and ship inside the APK. That is how
# Supabase is meant to be used: the publishable key identifies the project, not
# the player, and the row-level security in supabase/schema.sql is what keeps
# one player out of another's data. NEVER put the sb_secret_... key here — it
# bypasses every one of those rules.
#
# A build with these left empty still works: it plays entirely offline, with no
# gate and no friends, and says so in Settings.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your-publishable-key
